-Figure~\ref{fig:architecture} shows the DGF architecture. The two $A/E$ channels share encoder weights. The time--frequency branch represents a complex Morlet CWT by its modulus and argument. The Morlet parameter is $\mu=13.4$. The first bank uses scales $a=1,2,\ldots,16$, with reflection padding and $L^1$ normalization. Its nominal center frequencies are $\mu f_s/(2\pi a)$: scales 5--16 peak between 0.853 and 0.267 Hz, while scales 1--4 have centers above Nyquist. Retaining every fourth time sample gives a $2\times16\times264$ feature array per channel. Mixing along the temporal, feature and scale axes, followed by convolutional embedding and linear projection, produces $8\times32\times64$ features.
